\section{Discussion}
\label{sec:discussion}

\paragraph{CIVO mechanism.}
\looseness=-1 CIVO propagates through multiple pathways: Walker Walk develops a $1.63\times$ reward prediction gap while Cheetah Run shows none ($1.00\times$) despite higher severity ($8.27\times$ NVE). In Cheetah, observation fidelity reverses ($0.93\times$; $\dt{=}2$ predictions more accurate) while embedding geometry separates comparably (cosine ${\leq}{-}0.84$), suggesting CIVO propagates through latent-space dynamics rather than reward prediction; a random-policy decomposition attributes ${\approx}36\%$ of overestimation to dynamics bias and ${\approx}64\%$ to actor exploitation (Appendix~\ref{sec:civo_mechanism}). The mechanism is analogous to delusional bias \citep{lu2018nondelusional} but model-induced; unlike MPC, imagination-based actor-critic bootstraps value targets entirely within the learned model without real-data correction (Appendix~\ref{sec:mpc_immune}). Frozen embeddings participate identically in the forward pass yet never trigger CIVO (0/16 controls vs.\ 5/7 trained, $p < 0.001$; Table~\ref{tab:causal_ablation}): the vulnerability lies in what the embedding \emph{learns}, not in conditioning architecture.

